    "innovation": "This paper demonstrates that reducing black carbon emissions results in a much weaker-than-expected decline in global surface air temperatures, as its strong radiative forcing is largely compensated for by rapid atmospheric adjustments, making it a less effective climate mitigation measure compared to controlling sulphate aerosols.",
